window.bookSummaryJSON = "<p>In a world where divine beings and mortals coexist, Azreal, the formidable angel of death, finds himself at a crossroads of duty and desire. Tasked with delivering divine justice and collecting the souls of the marked, Azreal has always been bound by his celestial obligations. However, as his chains begin to loosen, he experiences the stirring of free will for the first time.</p> <p>This newfound autonomy leads him to discover an unexpected and profound connection with Alice, a mortal woman whose compassion and courage captivated him. The proposal of their love raises questions that challenge the celestial order: Can Alice accept Azreal's true nature with all of its supernatural responsibilities and burdens? and more pressingly, will the Gods, who have long dictated the course of angels and their fates, allow such a union to blossom?</p> <p>As Azreal grapples with these dilemmas, he must navigate the trials of love and judgment, discovering whether love can indeed transcend the boundaries of the divine and the mortal realms.</p>"; 
